<div class="header">
  <div class="header-inner">
    <div class="badge">📺 Sheryians Coding School · Sarthak Sharma</div>
    <h1>Learn <span class="html">HTML</span>, <span class="css">CSS</span> &amp; <span class="js">JavaScript</span> — Placement Notes</h1>
    <div class="header-meta">
      <span>⏱ 3h 53m</span>
      <span>📅 Sept 2024</span>
      <span>🎯 MERN Stack Basics</span>
      <span>👤 Placement-Ready</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tabs">
      <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab('overview',this)">Overview</button>
      <button class="tab-btn html-tab" onclick="switchTab('html',this)">HTML</button>
      <button class="tab-btn css-tab" onclick="switchTab('css',this)">CSS</button>
      <button class="tab-btn js-tab" onclick="switchTab('js',this)">JavaScript</button>
      <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab('interview',this)">🎯 Interview Q&amp;A</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<!-- ===== OVERVIEW ===== -->
<div id="tab-overview" class="tab-panel active">
  <div class="overview-grid">
    <div class="ov-card"><div class="ov-label" style="color:var(--html)">HTML</div><div class="ov-val" style="color:var(--html)">Structure</div><div class="ov-sub">Skeleton of the web page</div></div>
    <div class="ov-card"><div class="ov-label" style="color:var(--css)">CSS</div><div class="ov-val" style="color:var(--css)">Style</div><div class="ov-sub">Visual design & layout</div></div>
    <div class="ov-card"><div class="ov-label" style="color:var(--js)">JS</div><div class="ov-val" style="color:var(--js)">Behaviour</div><div class="ov-sub">Logic, interactivity, DOM</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header open" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">📌</div>
      <div class="section-title">What is the MERN Stack?</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body open">
      <p class="intro-text">MERN stands for <strong>MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, Node.js</strong> — a full-stack JavaScript framework for building modern web apps end-to-end. This video covers the frontend fundamentals needed before diving deeper.</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th><th>Role</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Database</td><td><code>MongoDB</code></td><td>NoSQL database — stores JSON-like documents</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Backend</td><td><code>Express.js</code></td><td>Web framework for Node.js — handles routing & APIs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Frontend</td><td><code>React.js</code></td><td>UI library — component-based view layer</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Runtime</td><td><code>Node.js</code></td><td>JS runtime — runs JavaScript outside the browser</td></tr>
      </table>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> Always explain MERN as "a JavaScript-only stack where the same language is used on both client and server, reducing context switching and improving team efficiency."</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header open" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">🌐</div>
      <div class="section-title">How the Web Works — Browser Basics</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body open">
      <ul>
        <li>User types a URL → DNS resolves it to an IP → HTTP request sent to server</li>
        <li>Server responds with HTML → browser parses it → builds the <strong>DOM tree</strong></li>
        <li>CSS is parsed → <strong>CSSOM</strong> is built → merged with DOM to create the <strong>Render Tree</strong></li>
        <li>JavaScript is fetched and executed → can manipulate DOM and CSSOM</li>
        <li>Browser performs <strong>Layout → Paint → Composite</strong> to display the page</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> Know the critical rendering path — it's a common performance interview question.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== HTML ===== -->
<div id="tab-html" class="tab-panel">

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header open" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">01</div>
      <div class="section-title">What is HTML?</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body open">
      <p class="intro-text html-border">HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the standard language for creating web pages. It describes the structure of a page using elements represented by tags.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>HTML is <strong>not</strong> a programming language — it's a <em>markup language</em></li>
        <li>Every HTML document starts with <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</code> — tells browser to use HTML5</li>
        <li>Root element is <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, containing <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> (metadata) and <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> (visible content)</li>
        <li>Elements are made of: <strong>Opening tag + Content + Closing tag</strong></li>
        <li>Some elements are <strong>self-closing</strong>: <code>&lt;br&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;hr&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;input&gt;</code></li>
      </ul>
      <pre><code><span class="cm">&lt;!-- Basic HTML structure --&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;html</span> <span class="attr">lang</span>=<span class="val">"en"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;head&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;meta</span> <span class="attr">charset</span>=<span class="val">"UTF-8"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;title&gt;</span>Page Title<span class="tag">&lt;/title&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;/head&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span>Hello World<span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">02</div>
      <div class="section-title">HTML Tags — Complete Reference</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h3>Headings & Text</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Note</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;h1&gt; – &lt;h6&gt;</code></td><td>Headings (largest to smallest)</td><td>Only one <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> per page (SEO)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;p&gt;</code></td><td>Paragraph</td><td>Block-level element</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;span&gt;</code></td><td>Inline text container</td><td>No semantic meaning, inline</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;strong&gt;</code></td><td>Bold + semantic importance</td><td>vs <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> which is just visual bold</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;em&gt;</code></td><td>Italic + emphasis</td><td>vs <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> which is just visual italic</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;br&gt;</code></td><td>Line break</td><td>Self-closing</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;hr&gt;</code></td><td>Horizontal rule</td><td>Thematic break</td></tr>
      </table>

      <h3>Links & Media</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Key Attributes</th><th>Note</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;a&gt;</code></td><td><code>href</code>, <code>target</code></td><td><code>target="_blank"</code> opens in new tab</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></td><td><code>src</code>, <code>alt</code>, <code>width</code>, <code>height</code></td><td><code>alt</code> is mandatory for accessibility</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;video&gt;</code></td><td><code>src</code>, <code>controls</code>, <code>autoplay</code></td><td>Needs <code>controls</code> for user playback</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;audio&gt;</code></td><td><code>src</code>, <code>controls</code></td><td>Same as video</td></tr>
      </table>

      <h3>Lists</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> — Unordered list (bullets) → contains <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> items</li>
        <li><code>&lt;ol&gt;</code> — Ordered list (numbered) → contains <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> items</li>
        <li><code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> — Definition list → uses <code>&lt;dt&gt;</code> (term) and <code>&lt;dd&gt;</code> (description)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Tables</h3>
      <pre><code><span class="tag">&lt;table&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;</span>Name<span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;</span>Age<span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;tbody&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;</span>Alice<span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;</span>25<span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;/tbody&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/table&gt;</span></code></pre>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> Know the difference between <code>&lt;th&gt;</code> (table header — bold, centered by default) and <code>&lt;td&gt;</code> (table data). Also know <code>colspan</code> and <code>rowspan</code> attributes.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">03</div>
      <div class="section-title">Semantic HTML</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="intro-text html-border">Semantic elements clearly describe their meaning both to the browser and the developer. They improve SEO and accessibility.</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Semantic Tag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;header&gt;</code></td><td>Top section — logo, nav, intro</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;nav&gt;</code></td><td>Navigation links</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;main&gt;</code></td><td>Primary content of the page (only one per page)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;section&gt;</code></td><td>Thematic grouping of content with a heading</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;article&gt;</code></td><td>Self-contained content (blog post, news item)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;aside&gt;</code></td><td>Sidebar or tangentially related content</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;footer&gt;</code></td><td>Bottom section — copyright, links</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;figure&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code></td><td>Images with captions</td></tr>
      </table>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> "Semantic HTML helps screen readers, search engines, and other tools understand your content. <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> have no semantic value."</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">04</div>
      <div class="section-title">HTML Forms</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="intro-text html-border">Forms collect user input and send it to a server. Key attributes: <code>action</code> (URL to send data) and <code>method</code> (GET or POST).</p>
      <pre><code><span class="tag">&lt;form</span> <span class="attr">action</span>=<span class="val">"/submit"</span> <span class="attr">method</span>=<span class="val">"POST"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;label</span> <span class="attr">for</span>=<span class="val">"name"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>Name:<span class="tag">&lt;/label&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"text"</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"name"</span> <span class="attr">name</span>=<span class="val">"name"</span> <span class="attr">required</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
  
  <span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"email"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Email"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"password"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"checkbox"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> Remember me
  <span class="tag">&lt;select&gt;&lt;option&gt;</span>Option 1<span class="tag">&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;textarea</span> <span class="attr">rows</span>=<span class="val">"4"</span><span class="tag">&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"submit"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>Submit<span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/form&gt;</span></code></pre>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Input Type</th><th>Use Case</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>text</code></td><td>Plain text input</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>email</code></td><td>Validates email format</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>password</code></td><td>Hides characters</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>number</code></td><td>Numeric input with min/max</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>checkbox</code></td><td>True/false toggle</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>radio</code></td><td>One-of-many selection</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>file</code></td><td>File upload</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>range</code></td><td>Slider</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>date</code></td><td>Date picker</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>hidden</code></td><td>Invisible data passed to server</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num html-num">05</div>
      <div class="section-title">Block vs Inline Elements & DOM</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <table>
        <tr><th></th><th>Block Elements</th><th>Inline Elements</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Behaviour</td><td>Start on a new line, take full width</td><td>Flow within text, take only needed width</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Examples</td><td><code>div, p, h1–h6, ul, table, section</code></td><td><code>span, a, img, strong, em, input</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Width/Height</td><td>Can be set</td><td>Cannot be set (use <code>display: inline-block</code>)</td></tr>
      </table>
      <hr class="divider">
      <h3>The DOM (Document Object Model)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The DOM is a tree-like representation of the HTML document in memory</li>
        <li>Every HTML element becomes a <strong>node</strong> in the DOM tree</li>
        <li>JavaScript uses the DOM API to <strong>read, create, update, and delete</strong> elements</li>
        <li>The root is <code>document</code> → children are <code>html</code> → <code>head</code>, <code>body</code> etc.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== CSS ===== -->
<div id="tab-css" class="tab-panel">

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header open" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">01</div>
      <div class="section-title">CSS Basics — Selectors & Properties</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body open">
      <p class="intro-text css-border">CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) controls the visual presentation of HTML. Styles can be applied inline, via a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> tag, or via an external <code>.css</code> file (preferred).</p>
      <h3>Selectors</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Selector</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Targets</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Universal</td><td><code>*</code></td><td>All elements</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Element</td><td><code>p</code></td><td>All &lt;p&gt; tags</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Class</td><td><code>.card</code></td><td>Elements with class="card"</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ID</td><td><code>#hero</code></td><td>Element with id="hero"</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Descendant</td><td><code>div p</code></td><td>&lt;p&gt; inside &lt;div&gt;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Child</td><td><code>ul > li</code></td><td>Direct &lt;li&gt; children of &lt;ul&gt;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Adjacent</td><td><code>h1 + p</code></td><td>&lt;p&gt; immediately after &lt;h1&gt;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Attribute</td><td><code>input[type="text"]</code></td><td>Inputs with that attribute</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pseudo-class</td><td><code>a:hover</code>, <code>li:first-child</code></td><td>State or position-based</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pseudo-element</td><td><code>p::before</code>, <code>p::after</code></td><td>Virtual sub-elements</td></tr>
      </table>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> CSS specificity order: <code>inline styles > ID > class/pseudo-class > element</code>. Specificity is calculated as (0,0,0,0) — (inline, id, class, element) counts.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">02</div>
      <div class="section-title">The Box Model</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="intro-text css-border">Every HTML element is a rectangular box. The box model defines how the space around elements is calculated.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="cm">/* From inside out: */</span>
<span class="cm">/* Content → Padding → Border → Margin */</span>

.box {
  width: <span class="num">200px</span>;       <span class="cm">/* Content area */</span>
  padding: <span class="num">20px</span>;      <span class="cm">/* Space inside border */</span>
  border: <span class="num">2px</span> solid red; <span class="cm">/* The border line */</span>
  margin: <span class="num">10px</span>;       <span class="cm">/* Space outside border */</span>
  box-sizing: border-box; <span class="cm">/* Total width = 200px */</span>
}</code></pre>
      <ul>
        <li><code>box-sizing: content-box</code> (default) — width = content only; padding & border are extra</li>
        <li><code>box-sizing: border-box</code> — width includes padding + border (recommended, more intuitive)</li>
        <li>Margins can <strong>collapse</strong> — two vertical margins merge into the larger one</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">03</div>
      <div class="section-title">Display & Positioning</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h3>Display</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Value</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>block</code></td><td>Full width, new line</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>inline</code></td><td>Inline flow, no width/height</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>inline-block</code></td><td>Inline flow but accepts width/height</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>none</code></td><td>Element removed from layout (invisible + no space)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>flex</code></td><td>Activates Flexbox on the element</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>grid</code></td><td>Activates CSS Grid on the element</td></tr>
      </table>
      <h3>Position</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Value</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>static</code></td><td>Default — normal document flow</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>relative</code></td><td>Offset from its normal position; still in flow</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>absolute</code></td><td>Removed from flow; positioned relative to nearest non-static ancestor</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>fixed</code></td><td>Stays fixed relative to viewport; removed from flow</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>sticky</code></td><td>Acts like relative until scroll threshold, then fixed</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">04</div>
      <div class="section-title">Flexbox</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="intro-text css-border">Flexbox is a 1D layout model that arranges items in a row or column. Applied on the <strong>parent container</strong>.</p>
      <pre><code>.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;        <span class="cm">/* row | column | row-reverse */</span>
  justify-content: center;    <span class="cm">/* main axis alignment */</span>
  align-items: center;        <span class="cm">/* cross axis alignment */</span>
  flex-wrap: wrap;            <span class="cm">/* allow items to wrap */</span>
  gap: <span class="num">16px</span>;               <span class="cm">/* spacing between items */</span>
}

.item {
  flex: <span class="num">1</span>;                  <span class="cm">/* grow + shrink + basis */</span>
  align-self: flex-start;     <span class="cm">/* override align-items for one */</span>
}</code></pre>
      <table>
        <tr><th>justify-content</th><th>Effect on Main Axis</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>flex-start</code></td><td>Pack to start</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>flex-end</code></td><td>Pack to end</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>center</code></td><td>Center items</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>space-between</code></td><td>Equal space between items, none at edges</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>space-around</code></td><td>Equal space around each item</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>space-evenly</code></td><td>Truly equal space everywhere</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">05</div>
      <div class="section-title">CSS Grid</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="intro-text css-border">Grid is a 2D layout system — controls rows AND columns simultaneously.</p>
      <pre><code>.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(<span class="num">3</span>, <span class="num">1fr</span>); <span class="cm">/* 3 equal columns */</span>
  grid-template-rows: auto;
  gap: <span class="num">20px</span>;
}

<span class="cm">/* Span across columns/rows */</span>
.hero { grid-column: <span class="num">1</span> / <span class="num">3</span>; } <span class="cm">/* from line 1 to 3 */</span>
.sidebar { grid-row: <span class="num">1</span> / <span class="num">3</span>; }</code></pre>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> "Use Flexbox for 1D layouts (a navbar, a row of cards). Use Grid for 2D layouts (full page layout, dashboards). They complement each other."</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">06</div>
      <div class="section-title">Responsive Design & Media Queries</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="cm">/* Mobile first: base styles for small screens */</span>
.container { width: <span class="num">100%</span>; }

<span class="cm">/* Tablet and up */</span>
@media (min-width: <span class="num">768px</span>) {
  .container { width: <span class="num">720px</span>; }
}

<span class="cm">/* Desktop and up */</span>
@media (min-width: <span class="num">1024px</span>) {
  .container { width: <span class="num">960px</span>; }
}</code></pre>
      <ul>
        <li>Common breakpoints: <code>480px</code> (mobile), <code>768px</code> (tablet), <code>1024px</code> (desktop), <code>1280px</code> (wide)</li>
        <li>Use <code>viewport meta tag</code>: <code>&lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"&gt;</code></li>
        <li>Use relative units: <code>%</code>, <code>em</code>, <code>rem</code>, <code>vw</code>, <code>vh</code> instead of fixed <code>px</code></li>
        <li><code>rem</code> — relative to root font-size (16px default). <code>em</code> — relative to parent element's font-size</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num css-num">07</div>
      <div class="section-title">CSS Variables & Animations</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="cm">/* CSS Custom Properties (Variables) */</span>
:root {
  --primary-color: #7c6af7;
  --font-size-lg: <span class="num">18px</span>;
}
.button { background: var(--primary-color); }

<span class="cm">/* Transitions */</span>
.btn { transition: all <span class="num">0.3s</span> ease; }
.btn:hover { transform: scale(<span class="num">1.05</span>); }

<span class="cm">/* Keyframe Animations */</span>
@keyframes fadeIn {
  from { opacity: <span class="num">0</span>; transform: translateY(<span class="num">20px</span>); }
  to   { opacity: <span class="num">1</span>; transform: translateY(<span class="num">0</span>); }
}
.hero { animation: fadeIn <span class="num">0.6s</span> ease forwards; }</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== JAVASCRIPT ===== -->
<div id="tab-js" class="tab-panel">

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header open" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num js-num">01</div>
      <div class="section-title">JS Basics — Variables & Data Types</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body open">
      <p class="intro-text js-border">JavaScript is a high-level, interpreted, dynamically-typed programming language. It runs in the browser and on the server (via Node.js).</p>
      <h3>Variable Declaration</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Keyword</th><th>Scope</th><th>Reassignable</th><th>Redeclarable</th><th>Hoisted</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>var</code></td><td>Function</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>✅ (as undefined)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>let</code></td><td>Block</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td><td>✅ (TDZ error)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>const</code></td><td>Block</td><td>❌</td><td>❌</td><td>✅ (TDZ error)</td></tr>
      </table>
      <h3>Data Types</h3>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip chip-yellow">Number</span>
        <span class="chip chip-green">String</span>
        <span class="chip chip-purple">Boolean</span>
        <span class="chip chip-red">null</span>
        <span class="chip chip-blue">undefined</span>
        <span class="chip chip-yellow">Symbol</span>
        <span class="chip chip-green">BigInt</span>
        <span class="chip chip-red">Object (non-primitive)</span>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="kw">typeof</span> <span class="str">"hello"</span>       <span class="cm">// "string"</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> <span class="num">42</span>            <span class="cm">// "number"</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> <span class="kw">true</span>          <span class="cm">// "boolean"</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> <span class="kw">undefined</span>     <span class="cm">// "undefined"</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> <span class="kw">null</span>          <span class="cm">// "object" ← famous JS bug!</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> {}            <span class="cm">// "object"</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> []            <span class="cm">// "object" (use Array.isArray())</span>
<span class="kw">typeof</span> <span class="fn">function</span>(){}  <span class="cm">// "function"</span></code></pre>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> <code>typeof null === "object"</code> is a known bug in JS from its origin. Always use <code>Array.isArray()</code> to check arrays since <code>typeof []</code> returns <code>"object"</code>.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num js-num">02</div>
      <div class="section-title">Functions — All Forms</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="cm">// 1. Function Declaration (hoisted)</span>
<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">greet</span>(name) {
  <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">`Hello, ${name}!`</span>;
}

<span class="cm">// 2. Function Expression (not hoisted)</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> greet = <span class="kw">function</span>(name) { <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">`Hi ${name}`</span>; };

<span class="cm">// 3. Arrow Function (ES6) — no own 'this'</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> <span class="fn">greet</span> = (name) => <span class="str">`Hey ${name}`</span>;
<span class="kw">const</span> <span class="fn">double</span> = n => n * <span class="num">2</span>;         <span class="cm">// implicit return</span>

<span class="cm">// 4. Default Parameters</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> <span class="fn">add</span> = (a, b = <span class="num">0</span>) => a + b;

<span class="cm">// 5. Rest Parameters</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> <span class="fn">sum</span> = (...nums) => nums.<span class="fn">reduce</span>((a,b) => a+b, <span class="num">0</span>);

<span class="cm">// 6. IIFE (Immediately Invoked)</span>
(<span class="kw">function</span>() { console.<span class="fn">log</span>(<span class="str">"runs immediately"</span>); })();</code></pre>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> Arrow functions don't have their own <code>this</code> — they inherit from the enclosing lexical scope. This is crucial for event handlers and class methods.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num js-num">03</div>
      <div class="section-title">Arrays & Array Methods</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="kw">const</span> nums = [<span class="num">1</span>, <span class="num">2</span>, <span class="num">3</span>, <span class="num">4</span>, <span class="num">5</span>];

<span class="cm">// map — transform each item, returns new array</span>
nums.<span class="fn">map</span>(n => n * <span class="num">2</span>)         <span class="cm">// [2,4,6,8,10]</span>

<span class="cm">// filter — keep items that pass test</span>
nums.<span class="fn">filter</span>(n => n > <span class="num">2</span>)      <span class="cm">// [3,4,5]</span>

<span class="cm">// reduce — accumulate to single value</span>
nums.<span class="fn">reduce</span>((acc, n) => acc + n, <span class="num">0</span>)  <span class="cm">// 15</span>

<span class="cm">// find / findIndex</span>
nums.<span class="fn">find</span>(n => n > <span class="num">3</span>)        <span class="cm">// 4</span>
nums.<span class="fn">findIndex</span>(n => n > <span class="num">3</span>)   <span class="cm">// 3</span>

<span class="cm">// forEach — side effect iteration (no return)</span>
nums.<span class="fn">forEach</span>(n => console.<span class="fn">log</span>(n));

<span class="cm">// some / every</span>
nums.<span class="fn">some</span>(n => n > <span class="num">4</span>)        <span class="cm">// true</span>
nums.<span class="fn">every</span>(n => n > <span class="num">0</span>)       <span class="cm">// true</span>

<span class="cm">// flat / flatMap</span>
[<span class="num">1</span>, [<span class="num">2</span>, [<span class="num">3</span>]]].<span class="fn">flat</span>(<span class="num">2</span>)          <span class="cm">// [1,2,3]</span>

<span class="cm">// Spread & Destructuring</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> copy = [...nums];
<span class="kw">const</span> [first, second, ...rest] = nums;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num js-num">04</div>
      <div class="section-title">Objects & ES6 Features</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="cm">// Object literal</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> user = { name: <span class="str">"Alice"</span>, age: <span class="num">25</span>, city: <span class="str">"Delhi"</span> };

<span class="cm">// Destructuring</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> { name, age } = user;
<span class="kw">const</span> { name: userName } = user;   <span class="cm">// rename on destructure</span>

<span class="cm">// Spread</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> updated = { ...user, age: <span class="num">26</span> };

<span class="cm">// Optional Chaining (?.) — ES2020</span>
user?.address?.city   <span class="cm">// undefined instead of error</span>

<span class="cm">// Nullish Coalescing (??) — ES2020</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> name = user.name ?? <span class="str">"Guest"</span>;  <span class="cm">// only null/undefined</span>

<span class="cm">// Shorthand properties & computed keys</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> x = <span class="num">10</span>, y = <span class="num">20</span>;
<span class="kw">const</span> point = { x, y };             <span class="cm">// { x: 10, y: 20 }</span>

<span class="cm">// Object methods</span>
Object.<span class="fn">keys</span>(user)    <span class="cm">// ["name","age","city"]</span>
Object.<span class="fn">values</span>(user)  <span class="cm">// ["Alice",25,"Delhi"]</span>
Object.<span class="fn">entries</span>(user) <span class="cm">// [["name","Alice"],...]</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num js-num">05</div>
      <div class="section-title">DOM Manipulation</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="cm">// Selecting Elements</span>
document.<span class="fn">getElementById</span>(<span class="str">"id"</span>)
document.<span class="fn">querySelector</span>(<span class="str">".class"</span>)       <span class="cm">// first match</span>
document.<span class="fn">querySelectorAll</span>(<span class="str">"div"</span>)      <span class="cm">// NodeList of all</span>

<span class="cm">// Changing Content</span>
el.textContent = <span class="str">"Hello"</span>;              <span class="cm">// plain text (safe)</span>
el.innerHTML = <span class="str">"&lt;b&gt;Bold&lt;/b&gt;"</span>;          <span class="cm">// parses HTML (XSS risk)</span>

<span class="cm">// Changing Styles & Classes</span>
el.style.color = <span class="str">"red"</span>;
el.classList.<span class="fn">add</span>(<span class="str">"active"</span>);
el.classList.<span class="fn">remove</span>(<span class="str">"hidden"</span>);
el.classList.<span class="fn">toggle</span>(<span class="str">"open"</span>);

<span class="cm">// Attributes</span>
el.<span class="fn">setAttribute</span>(<span class="str">"src"</span>, <span class="str">"img.png"</span>);
el.<span class="fn">getAttribute</span>(<span class="str">"href"</span>);

<span class="cm">// Creating & Appending</span>
<span class="kw">const</span> div = document.<span class="fn">createElement</span>(<span class="str">"div"</span>);
div.textContent = <span class="str">"New element"</span>;
document.body.<span class="fn">appendChild</span>(div);

<span class="cm">// Removing</span>
el.<span class="fn">remove</span>();</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection(this)">
      <div class="section-num js-num">06</div>
      <div class="section-title">Events</div>
      <span class="section-arrow">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <pre><code><span class="cm">// addEventListener (preferred)</span>
btn.<span class="fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="str">"click"</span>, <span class="kw">function</span>(e) {
  e.<span class="fn">preventDefault</span>();   <span class="cm">// stop default action (e.g. form submit)</span>
  e.<span class="fn">stopPropagation</span>(); <span class="cm">// stop event from bubbling up</span>
  console.<span class="fn">log</span>(e.target); <span class="cm">// element that was clicked</span>
});

<span class="cm">// Event Delegation — attach one listener to parent</span>
document.<span class="fn">querySelector</span>(<span class="str">"ul"</span>).<span class="fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="str">"click"</span>, e => {
  <span class="kw">if</span> (e.target.tagName === <span class="str">"LI"</span>) console.<span class="fn">log</span>(e.target.textContent);
});</code></pre>
      <h3>Common Events</h3>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip chip-yellow">click</span>
        <span class="chip chip-yellow">dblclick</span>
        <span class="chip chip-yellow">mouseover</span>
        <span class="chip chip-yellow">mouseout</span>
        <span class="chip chip-green">keydown</span>
        <span class="chip chip-green">keyup</span>
        <span class="chip chip-green">keypress</span>
        <span class="chip chip-blue">submit</span>
        <span class="chip chip-blue">input</span>
        <span class="chip chip-blue">change</span>
        <span class="chip chip-purple">DOMContentLoaded</span>
        <span class="chip chip-purple">load</span>
        <span class="chip chip-red">scroll</span>
        <span class="chip chip-red">resize</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tip"><strong>🎯 Interview tip:</strong> Event <strong>bubbling</strong> — events bubble up from child → parent → document. Event <strong>capturing</strong> — fires from document down to target (set 3rd arg of addEventListener to <code>true</code>).</div>
